 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For the following problems, recall that the SAT exam has mean 1060 and standard deviation 195, and that composite scores on the ACT have mean 21 and standard deviation 5. ",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 528657,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "At what percentile would an SAT score of 940 fall? Round to the nearest whole number.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In an empty cell of Google Sheets, use the function NORM.DIST.</p>\n<p>NORM.DIST(your data value, your mean, your standard deviation, TRUE)</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(940, 1060, 195,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.2691503745</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 27<sup>th</sup> percentile</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "27th"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 528658,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What score would be at the 67th percentile on the ACT?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>When your data is normally distributed and you know the percentile, mean, and standard deviation, you can find the data value with the NORM.INV function.</p>\n<p>NORM.INV(percentile as a decimal, mean, standard deviation)</p>\n<p>Convert the 67<sup>th</sup> percentile to 0.67.</p>\n<p>In an empty cell in Google Sheets: =NORM.INV(0.67, 21, 5)</p>\n<p>You see: 23.19956583</p>\n<p>The approximate value: 23.2</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>23.2</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 528659,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which is a better score: 1300 on the SAT or 27 on the ACT?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In an empty cell of Google Sheets, use the function NORM.DIST.</p>\n<p>NORM.DIST(your data value, your mean, your standard deviation, TRUE)</p>\n<p>Find the percentile for the 1300 on the SAT.</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(1300, 1060, 195,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.8907954067</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 89.1<sup>st</sup> percentile</p>\n<p>Find the percentile for the 27 on the ACT.</p>\n<p>In an empty cell in Google Sheets: =NORM.DIST(27, 21, 5,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.8849303298</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 88.4<sup>th</sup> percentile</p>\n<p>The 1300 is at the 89.1st percentile while the 27 is at the 88.4<sup>th</sup> percentile. The 1300 on the SAT is the better score.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>1300 on the SAT</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
